      "answer": "$B$ rebounds at $0.5\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$; the combined particle has speed $3.03\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ down the plane (exactly $91/30\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$).",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "For either particle, $mg\\sin30^\\circ=ma$ with sign according to the chosen direction; specifically $0.4g\\sin30^\\circ=0.4a$ for $A$, $0.2g\\sin30^\\circ=0.2a$ for $B$, or $mg\\sin30^\\circ=ma$. — M1: allow sine/cosine mix.\n$a=\\pm5$ or $\\pm g\\sin30^\\circ$. — A1; allow $g\\sin30^\\circ$ without working for M1A1.\nFor $B$ when it hits the barrier: $v^2=3^2+2(5)(1.6)$, giving $v=5$. — M1: use their $a\\ne\\pm g$ and their $v$ from part (a).\nAlternative: $v=3+5(0.4)$, giving $v=5$. — M1: use their $a\\ne\\pm g$ and their $v$ from part (a).\nAlternative average-speed method: $1.6=\\frac{3+v}{2}(0.4)$, giving $v=5$. — M1.\nAlternative energy method: $\\tfrac12(0.2)v^2-\\tfrac12(0.2)(3^2)=0.2(1.6)g\\sin30^\\circ$. — M1.\nSpeed after hitting barrier $=0.1(5)=0.5\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$. — A1 AG.\n$v_A=2.5+5(0.44)=4.7$ and $v_B=-0.5+5(0.04)=-0.3$, or $v_B=0.5+(-5)(0.04)=0.3$. — *M1: use $v=u+at$ for either with the correct time, an initial speed of $2.5$ or $\\pm0.5$, and their acceleration $\\ne\\pm g$.\n$0.4(4.7)+0.2(-0.3)=0.6v_{\\mathrm{comb}}$. — DM1: use $v=u+at$ for both with correct times, initial speeds and the same acceleration, then conservation of momentum with the correct number of terms; allow sign errors.\n$v_{\\mathrm{comb}}=3.03\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$. — A1; allow $91/30$; allow DM1A0 if $g$ is included with the masses.\nTotal: 7.",
